{"text": "Brennecke & Oyama, CPAs\n\n2140 NE Halsey Street, Suite 300 · Portland, Oregon 97232\n\nMarch 9, 2026\n\nVIA SECURE PORTAL AND FIRST-CLASS MAIL\n\nLeilani Kapule-Stroud, Trustee\n\nKapule-Stroud Living Trust u/a/d 6/14/2011\n\nPO Box 2291\n\nHood River, OR 97031\n\nRe: 2025 Schedule K-1 (Form 1065), Wapato Flats Hop Growers, LP\n\nPartnership EIN 93-1284406; partner no. 017\n\nDear Ms. Kapule-Stroud:\n\nEnclosed is the Trust's 2025 Schedule K-1 from Wapato Flats (the \"Partnership\").\nThe K-1 was issued under the Trust's taxpayer identification number, which for a\ngrantor trust is your Social Security number, shown on the form as XXX-XX-6538.\nPlease confirm that the last four digits (6538) match your records; the prior-year\nK-1 was issued in error under the Trust's old EIN, 93-6019954.\n\nSummary of your share (limited partner, 4.25% of profit, loss and capital):\n\n Box 1, ordinary business income: $38,412\n Box 5, interest income: $207\n Box 19A, cash distributions: $22,000, paid 07/15/2025 and 12/19/2025 by ACH to\nthe account ending ...4471 at Mount Defiance Credit Union\n Box 20Z, Section 199A information: see Statement A\n Capital account (tax basis): beginning $311,906; ending $328,525\n\nState matters. The Partnership operates in Oregon and Washington (Yakima\nCounty). Your Washington-source share is $9,880; no Washington income tax\nreturn is required. The Partnership paid Oregon elective pass-through entity tax\n(PTE-E) of $3,457 on your behalf under OR BIN 1847729-5, which you may claim as\na credit on your Oregon individual return.\n\nPortal access. Your K-1 package is posted here:\n\nhttps://portal.brennecke-oyama.example/k1/WFHG-017\n\nSign in with user ID lkapulestroud; your one-time passcode is Hops-7731-Kiln and\nexpires in 14 days. If you are locked out, call Dev Rangarajan at 503-555-0139.\nPlease do not email the passcode.\n\nItems needing your attention:\n\n1. The general partner, Hop Hollow Management LLC, still shows your address of\nrecord as the Odell farmhouse (3390 Straight Hill Road). We gave them the PO\nbox.\n\n2. Burkhard Stoll of Hop Hollow advised that the $15,000 capital call noticed\nJanuary 30 is due April 1, 2026. Wire to Mount Defiance Credit Union, routing\n028784395, acct 70044180226, reference WFHG-CC-2026-017.\n\n3. The 0.75% interest formerly held by your late husband, Gordon Stroud (d.\n11/02/2024), was combined with the Trust's interest. Mr. Stoll confirms that the §\n754 basis step-up of $46,300 is reflected on Statement B. Gordon's final K-1 was\nsent to the estate's attorney.\n\nEstimated tax (Form 1040-ES). Based on the K-1 alone we project additional 2025\nfederal tax of about $8,900 and recommend a first-quarter 2026 estimate of $2,300\nby April 15. Our fee for the K-1 review is $450.00, invoice BO-26-1187.\n\nVery truly yours,\n\nNoriko Oyama, CPA (OR lic. 11482) · PTIN P01847720\n\nDirect (503) 555-0171 · noyama@brennecke-oyama.example\n\ncc: B. Stoll, Hop Hollow; file KAPULE-STROUD, L. / 2025-K1-0417", "kind": "PDF", "detail": "2 pages · 454 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Leilani Kapule-Stroud", "Burkhard Stoll", "Dev Rangarajan", "Gordon Stroud"], "companies": ["Brennecke & Oyama", "Wapato Flats Hop Growers, LP", "Mount Defiance Credit Union", "Hop Hollow Management LLC", "Kapule-Stroud Living Trust", "Oregon", "Washington", "Yakima County", "Brennecke-oyama"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Portland", "Oregon", "Hood River", "OR", "Yakima County", "Mount Defiance Credit Union", "Odell farmhouse", "Hop Hollow"], "health": [], "sensitive": ["Social Security number", "race or ethnicity", "religion", "political views or donations", "union membership", "sexual orientation", "immigration or citizenship status", "criminal history", "genetic information"], "names": ["Leilani", "Brennecke", "Oyama", "Hop Hollow", "Burkhard", "Gordon", "Noriko", "B"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 73.40000000223517, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 30